# One person, one identity. GitHub builds noreply addresses as <id>+<login>@users.noreply.github.com,
# and a renamed git identity leaves both spellings in history. Without this, `git shortlog -sne` shows
# the same person twice and a leaderboard can credit work to a phantom.
MCPVOT <mcpvot@users.noreply.github.com> <22164026+MCPVOT@users.noreply.github.com>
MCPVOT <mcpvot@users.noreply.github.com> VOT <22164026+MCPVOT@users.noreply.github.com>
